    {
      "id": "7c48d1a381b24f6462a565fec9b6ed965f20e217",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 680949079,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> HAVE_SMI_VERSION_STRING is always defined if libsmi found\n\nIf `ENABLE_SMI` is false, it shouldn't look for libsmi in the first place, as the user has indicated that they don't want Wireshark linked with it.  If it's finding libsmi when `ENABLE_SMI` is false, that's a bug.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-17T20:11:59.259Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-17T20:11:59.259Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117321943,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4221,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7d2a9671f7e7e1332befb5e6665676ac7b51945f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 680988909,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The better fix would be to address the fact that `HAVE_SMI_VERSION_STRING` is supposedly \"always defined\", which I find unlikely.\n\n```\n$ cmake -DENABLE_SMI=Off ..\n$ grep HAVE_SMI config.h\n/* #undef HAVE_SMI_VERSION_STRING */\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-17T21:15:50.138Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-18T09:01:12.757Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117321943,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4221,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ef786b7fe9d352108ed0e22344cd17c209640586",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 680990750,
          "type": null,
          "body": "By the way this check was added because by default `extern` variables are not visible on Windows and that's what the libsmi code uses. My commit message should have mentioned that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
